8.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The forced initial forcing is 1.W B2 2.B B1. 2.B B1 is forced because after 1.W B2 the C1–C2 chain has the unique liberty B1 and the white B2 stone has the unique liberty B1. After 2.B B1 the three black fragments are

* X = B1C1C2  {A1,B2}
* Y = A2      {A1,A3,B2}
* Z = B3B4    {A3,A4,B2}

with the four relevant empty points A1, A3, A4, B2.  A1 is illegal for White and B2 is illegal for White, so the only local net moves are A3/A4.

3.W A3 is met by 4.B A4 capturing A3 and by 4.B B2 connecting X,Y,Z to M with liberties A1,A4 and White A3 with the unique liberty A4; 4.B B2 5.W A4 gives White A3–A4 with the unique liberty A5 and M with the unique liberty A1.  Black 6.B A5 now captures the white A3–A4 group, A3 and A4 become empty again and M regains the liberties A1,A3,A4.  The same capture appears after 3.W A4 4.B B2 5.W A3.  In the B2 line the defence 6.B A5 is always available because the white net A3–A4 has A5 as its only outside liberty and A5 is empty and adjacent to B5 w.

The B1 first move is also not killing. After 1.W B1 black can legally play 2.B B2 and connect A2,B3,B4,C1,C2; the merged group then has the three liberties A1,A3,A4 and White B1 is in atari on A1.  The B2 move is not suicide: after the connection the group has A1,A3,A4.  The subsequent net 3.W A3 4.B A1 captures White B1 or 4.B A4 captures White A3, and again 5...A5 can be used to capture a white A3–A4 net.

Hence every local first move is met by a Black capture or connection that restores at least one liberty, and the A5 capture of any white A3–A4 net is the decisive defence.  The suicide claim for 2...B2 after 1.W B1 used in the Colleague 4/9 lines is false; the move is legal via the merged group liberties A1,A3,A4.  With the A5 defence the B2 and B1 first moves are not forcing kills.

Current best belief: no first move initiates a forced capture, i.e. {}.

